X:1
T:The Holly and the Ivy
C:Traditional English
O:England
S:Melody: traditional English carol (public domain), checked note by note against the Mutopia Project edition in this repo (sources/mutopia/thehollyandtheivy.ly, Mutopia-2005/12/23-644, public domain); a test compares the soprano voice with it
Z:Encoded for Go Go HarmoniYo by GitHub Copilot (agent, Claude Opus 5.5), 2026-10-25. The four-part harmony (alto, tenor, bass) and the chord symbols are our own, written for this repo; not taken from any published setting.
N:SATB, four voices: S = melody, A, T, B = our own plain hymn-style harmony (mostly one chord per beat, cadences F/C - C7 - F). Verse and refrain written out.
N:F major (B flat); one-beat pickup on F4; soprano range C4-D5, bass B flat 2-F3. Checked: soprano pitches and rhythm equal the Mutopia melody; every bar of every voice sums to 3 beats.
